# MRL family 5: multi-byte quantifier bodies, non-multiple subject lengths.
#
# (?:ab){3,6} has a 2-byte body; its true minimum is 3*2=6 bytes, and any
# valid match length must be a multiple of 2 within [6,12]. Subjects whose
# length is NOT a multiple of the body width, or that are one byte short
# of a legal boundary, are exactly where a bound computed per-repetition
# instead of per-byte (or vice versa) would land between two legal
# iteration boundaries and get the wrong answer.


# 2-byte body, min 3 reps = 6 bytes.
pattern (?:ab){3,6}
n "abab"
n "ababa"
m "ababab" 0 6
m "abababa" 0 6
m "abababab" 0 8
m "ababababababab" 0 12

# same multi-byte body, now with a trailing literal forcing an exact rep count at the match.
pattern (?:ab){3,6}c
n "ababc"
m "abababc" 0 7
m "abababababc" 0 11
m "ababababababababc" 4 17

# 3-byte body: min 2 reps = 6 bytes, not a multiple of 2.
pattern (?:abc){2,5}
n "abcab"
m "abcabc" 0 6
m "abcabca" 0 6
m "abcabcabc" 0 9
